content.text:
verdict: findings
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1 — decidable without the annex, result: fail, notes: "Ask 3's own text says 'main installs exactly 38 skills' but the Annex section calls its inventory 'the 36-skill inventory table'; resolving which count is right requires opening the annex. Cited: ask 3."}
  - {scenario: 2 — first paragraph answers, result: pass, notes: "Paragraph 1 states it outright: 'Recommendation: enrich the role-definition typedef with six sections... re-author the three roles through it, and import the skill catalogue by kind'."}
  - {scenario: 3 — no unintroduced terms, result: pass, notes: "External frameworks (RAPID, DACI, Scrum, Team Topologies, SFIA, Dean Peters' collection) are all glossed at first mention; remaining bare terms (typedef, Phase 1, the basis, definition chain, Bounded Context) read as recorded shop/product vocabulary the authority holds."}
  - {scenario: 4 — asks complete and honest about gating, result: pass, notes: "All four asks carry recommendation, inline evidence, and a default; gating is stated for the set ('Asks 1–3 gate the work; ask 4 defaults on silence') and per-ask."}
ask_decidability: ["ask 1: confident — sections and rules enumerated, evidence maps failure classes to sections, gating explicit", "ask 2: wobbly — the ask says to re-author three roles 'using the two old agent templates as source material', but the two templates named belong to architect and PO; the source material for lead-pm is never stated (paragraph 1 implies its content lived in 26 skills, but the ask does not say so)", "ask 3: wobbly — the bucket arithmetic in the ask sums cleanly to 38, but the annex is labeled a '36-skill inventory table', so I cannot tell whether the plan I am approving covers every installed file", "ask 4: confident — sourced evidence (main:adrs/adr-066.md, the grant, per-file notices), clear handling rule, default rides ask 3"]
overload: "right-sized — four asks, one page, evidence inline, research deferred to an optional annex"
stumbles: ["'and the 36-skill inventory table' (Annex section) against '`main` installs exactly 38 skills; the five buckets sum to it' (ask 3) — two different totals for the same inventory", "'The PM seat worked only because 26 skills carried its procedure' (paragraph 1) against ask 3's PM-attributable buckets (6 working-mode + 19 lenses = 25) — the 26th is unaccounted", "'using the two old agent templates as source material' (ask 2) — three roles are being re-authored from two templates, and neither template is the PM's", "'amend the role-definition typedef (v3)' (ask 1) — momentarily ambiguous whether v3 is the version being amended or the version the amendment produces; ask 2's 'the amended typedef (v3)' settles it only in retrospect"]
unintroduced_terms: []
top_changes: ["Reconcile the inventory totals: make the Annex line and ask 3 carry the same number (38), or state in the brief why the annex table holds 36 of the 38", "Reconcile the PM skill count: either correct '26 skills' in paragraph 1 or show in ask 3 where the count beyond 6+19 lives (e.g., among the generated writing skills)", "In ask 2, state the source material for lead-pm explicitly (the skill-carried procedure), since the two named templates cover only architect and PO"]
